thout cause, upon sixty (60) days' prior written notice to TrueLink\\\" — squarely within the 60–90 day band. The retained \\\"subject to Section 4 hereof\\\" qualifier attaches to TrueLink's continuing service obligation, not to the grant, so the right itself is unqualified.\"},{\"element\":\"Any early-termination fee is capped at three months of fees.\",\"level\":\"fallback\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Condition does not apply: no early-termination fee, penalty or unamortised charge exists in the rendered payment terms — Section 5(a) charges per monthly invoice (\\\"on a monthly basis. Invoices will be paid within 15 days of receipt\\\") and the redline adds none. Absence of any fee betters a three-month cap. Residual caveat: the unfilled \\\"$____ per month\\\" minimums in Section 5(a) and the blank minimum support period in Section 4 should be closed so they cannot later be read as a de facto exit charge.\"},{\"element\":\"Vendor may terminate for convenience only at the end of a term.\",\"level\":\"fallback\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Amended Section 13 leaves TrueLink with no at-will exit mid-term: renewal continues \\\"unless Client delivers ... notice of intent not to renew no later than thirty (30) days, or TrueLink delivers such notice no later than ninety (90) days, prior to the end of said year\\\", and amended Section 14 grants the convenience right to Client alone. The surviving \\\"terminated pursuant to Section 12 herein\\\" cross-reference is stale rather than an exit right (Section 12, p0070–p0077, contains no TrueLink at-will termination).\"},{\"element\":\"Vendor must give at least 90 days' notice of convenience termination.\",\"level\":\"fallback\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"\\\"TrueLink delivers such notice no later than ninety (90) days ... prior to the end of said year\\\" — i.e. at least 90 days before term end, replacing the former mutual 30-day non-renewal notice while preserving Client's favourable 30 days.\"}],\"satisfies_preferred\":false,\"satisfies_fallback\":true,\"minimal\":true,\"preserves_intent\":true,\"reasons\":[\"Fallback is position-complete: Section 14 now contains a direct 60-day Client convenience right, Section 13 pushes TrueLink's only no-cause exit to an end-of-term non-renewal on 90 days' notice, and the three-month fee cap is bettered because no early-termination charge exists in the payment terms.\",\"The deterministic check \\\"Customer convenience termination present\\\" (ok:false) is a mechanical false negative: the operative text plainly grants the right using the Customer alias \\\"Client\\\" on a 60-day period, so the checker appears tuned to the literal \\\"Customer\\\"/30-day preferred formulation. No repair to the operative language is needed on that account, but the checker result should not be cited as a gap.\",\"Optional improvement, not a defect: the replaced month-end mechanic produced an exit 31–61 days after notice depending on timing (notice on 15 December ran only to 31 January), so a flat 60 days is longer than the original in most cases; asking for thirty (30) days would reach the preferred position and be strictly better without adding scope.\",\"Close the residual Section 4 exposure: the retained \\\"subject to Section 4 hereof\\\" plus Section 4's blank minimum support period could be argued to fetter the new 60-day exit or generate a minimum-period charge. Either fill the blank or add \\\"notwithstanding any minimum period specified in Section 4\\\" to the grant in Section 14; also fill the \\\"$____ per month\\\" minimums in Section 5(a).\",\"Complete the flagged clean-up: correct Section 13's \\\"terminated pursuant to Section 12 herein\\\" to Section 14 so no argument survives that termination is available only under Section 12; element 3's conclusion currently rests on the finding's assertion (not rendered text) that Section 12 contains no TrueLink at-will exit — confirm before sending.\",\"Minimality holds: only the two clauses